id: pm-4vymxc
title: "PR1548: preserve rollback diagnostic provenance and reject non-directory ancestry"
description: "CodeRabbit full review of PR1548 identified two additional SDK boundary defects: physical initialization ancestry treats ENOTDIR as absence and can publish rules for an impossible tracker; a failed rollback wrapper discards the original typed refusal code and cause. Preserve the final rollback code and exit policy while retaining diagnostic provenance, and require ENOENT-only ancestry climbing. Delivery also corrects the reviewed recovery corpus typo and stale hosted-check metadata through the CLI."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: bug,review,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-22T12:58:46.665Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T14:45:58.047Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-22T14:45:56.751Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T14:45:56.751Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Real regular-file ancestry rejects without writing rules; Typed and untyped original rollback errors retain cause and only typed errors expose original code; Original recovery command and retained backup still execute; Source and metadata findings are resolved in the same reviewed PR
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Retained original rollback failure cause and optional typed original_code without changing generic exit behavior, rejected real non-directory ancestors across platforms, regenerated the emitted ENOTDIR SDK receipt, and corrected review-discovered alert and PM command/check evidence."
expected_result: "Failed rollback exposes recovery plus original failure provenance, while invalid file ancestry refuses before ignore writes on every supported platform; public SDK types and generated receipts agree."
actual_result: "Linked59 focused cases, public SDK type fixtures and native full acceptance pass. Windows direct-file and nested-file refusals preserve ignore bytes; Nightly39795091164 reports11035 passing cases and exact100/100/100/100. Five actionable review findings have concrete fixes and resolved threads, with subsequent full source review reporting none."
